# Firebase configuration (tracking only)
# 1. Copy this file to .env  (cp .env.example .env)
# 2. Firebase Console -> Project Settings -> Your apps -> Web app -> Config
# 3. Firebase Console -> Firestore Database -> Create database (production or test mode)
# 4. (Recommended) Firestore Rules for this demo:
#      rules_version = '2';
#      service cloud.firestore {
#        match /databases/{database}/documents {
#          match /shipments/{id} {
#            allow read: if true;
#            allow write: if true;   // tighten for production
#          }
#          match /activity/{id} {
#            allow read, write: if true;
#          }
#          match /admins/{email} {
#            allow read: if true;
#          }
#        }
#      }
# 5. Admin access: any Firebase Auth user whose email is in the 'admins'
#    Firestore collection (create a doc with the email as the document ID,
#    e.g. admins/admin@fedex.com). admin@fedex.com and adminmain@gmail.com
#    are always allowed.
# 6. Netlify: Site settings -> Environment variables -> add each VITE_* value, then redeploy

# Cloudflare Turnstile (bot gate on every page)
# 1. Create a free Cloudflare account at https://dash.cloudflare.com
# 2. Left sidebar -> Turnstile -> Add widget
#    - Widget name: anything
#    - Hostnames: your Vercel URL (e.g. mysite.vercel.app) + localhost for testing
#    - Widget Mode: Managed
# 3. Copy the Site Key and Secret Key below
# 4. Vercel: Project -> Settings -> Environment Variables ->
#    add TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY and TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY (all environments),
#    then redeploy. Until both are set, the gate lets everyone through (fail-open).
# 5. Test locally with `npx vercel dev` (middleware doesn't run in `npm run dev`)

TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=
TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=

VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=
VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=

# EmailJS email notifications (optional; emails sender + recipient on create/update)
# 1. Create a free account at https://www.emailjs.com
# 2. Email Services -> Add New Service (Gmail/Outlook/etc.)
# 3. Email Templates -> Create New Template. Use variables below, e.g.:
#      Subject: Your FedEx shipment {{tracking_number}} was {{action}}
#      Content: Hello {{to_name}}, {{status_description}}. Track: {{tracking_url}}
#      Available variables: to_name, tracking_number, tracking_url, action, status,
#      status_description, event_text, sender_name, recipient_name, origin,
#      destination, service, eta, date_time
#    IMPORTANT: in the template's "To Email" field put {{to_email}}
# 4. Account -> General: copy your Public Key (user_id)
# 5. In the same page, add your site URLs to "Allowed origins" (http://localhost:5173 and your Netlify URL)
